# vim cheatsheet — personal config reminders

---

## Leader
  **Leader = `<Space>`**

---

## File Operations
  `<leader>w`   Save
  `<leader>q`   Quit
  `:w` / `:q`   Standard save/quit

---

## Navigation
  **Relative line numbers** enabled
  **Cursorline** highlighted
  **Scrolloff=5** (5 lines context)

### Window splits
  `:split` / `:vsplit`   Split (opens **below/right** by default)

---

## Search
  `/` / `?`           Search forward/backward
  `<Esc><Esc>`        Clear search highlight
  `incsearch`          Incremental search (live as you type)
  `hlsearch`           Highlight matches
  `ignorecase` + `smartcase`  Case-insensitive unless uppercase present

### ripgrep integration
  `<leader>r`         `:Rg` — search project with ripgrep
  `:grep <pattern>`   Search, populate quickfix list
  `:copen` / `:cclose` Open/close quickfix list
  `:cdo %s/old/new/g` Replace across all matches

---
## fzf
  `<leader>f`   `:Files` — fuzzy find files
  `<leader>g`   `:GFiles` — fuzzy find git files
  `<leader>b`   `:Buffers` — fuzzy find open buffers

---
## Git (fugitive)
  `<leader>gs`  `:Git` — git status
  `<leader>gd`  `:Gdiffsplit` — diff against HEAD
  `<leader>gb`  `:Git blame` — show blame for current line
  `:Gcommit`     Commit
  `:Gpush`       Push

---
## Plugins

### surround
  `ys<motion><char>`    Wrap motion in char (e.g., `ysiw"` → wrap word in quotes)
  `cs<old><new>`         Change surrounding (e.g., `cs'"` → change " to ')
  `ds<char>`            Delete surrounding

### commentary
  `gc<motion>`          Toggle comment on motion (e.g., `gcj` comment line, `gcap` comment paragraph)
  `gcc`                 Toggle comment on current line (visual mode works too)

### unimpaired
  `[b` / `]b`           Previous / next buffer
  `[B` / `]B`           First / last buffer
  `[p` / `]p`           Previous / next positional mark
  `[<` / `]>`           Previous / next fold

### tmux-runner
  `<leader>vr`          Open tmux runner
  `<leader>vs`          Send current line/visual selection to tmux runner

---
## Settings & Behavior

### Indentation
  Default: **4 spaces** (expandtab)
  Go: **tabs** (noexpandtab, sw=4, ts=4)
  Python/JS/HTML/CSS/PHP/Shell: **2 spaces**

### Clipboard
  `"+y` / `"+p`          Yank to / paste from OS clipboard
  (Note: unnamed register **shares with clipboard** if +clipboard)

### UI
  `list` enabled         Show tabs as `▸`, trailing spaces as `·`, nbsp as `_`
  `noshowmode`          Mode shown in statusline, not in command area
  Custom statusline     Shows: mode, git branch, filename, flags, encoding, line:col, percentage

### Performance
  Files > **5MB**: no undo, no swap, no syntax (prevents lag on large files)

### Format on Save
  **Go**: auto-format with `gofmt` on save
  **Rust**: auto-format with `rustfmt` on save

---
## File Browser (netrw fallback)
  `:Explore` / `:Ex`     Open built-in file browser
  Banner disabled, liststyle=3

---
## Undo
  Persistent undo enabled (saved to `~/.vim/undo/`)
  `:undo` / `:redo`      Navigate undo history